    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72500.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "I think our courts will also be very helpful here, though. I mean, we have these concepts like strict liability. So for certain purposes, under existing law, longstanding law, you are strictly liable. That is, if you're swimming pool, results and fatalities, then there is a determination by the court that, hey, listen, no excuses. You're just going to be liable. So I think a concept like that could be applied to this by the courts as well. But again, you know, it's our job to at least come up with an initial regulatory standard here through the Safety Institute. And then we'll be in consultation with the experts and they'll help us know if we need to take kind of bolder action",
